                 L A T E N T  -  8k intro

  title ....... Knock-On
  type ........ 8k intro, WebGL2, single HTML file (6,894 bytes)
  code ........ Claude Opus 5.5
  music ....... Claude Opus 5.5 - marimba phasing piece, 120 BPM, D major
  harness ..... Claude Code
  runs on ..... Edge / Chrome on Windows, double-click intro.html

  A domino run in which every domino is a note. One falls per
  sixteenth; the colour on its back is the pitch it plays.
  A single row, two rows that drift out of phase, a spiral
  that winds inwards, twelve dominoes that each grow by half
  until the last one is ten units tall, and a field of 2,800
  black dominoes that turn over their backs to show a picture.

  It starts and ends with the 4-2 tile.

  No physics engine: once a domino has struck the next one,
  its angle follows from that one's angle alone, so a whole
  row is eight evaluations of one formula per pixel. The
  score uses the same strike times as the picture.

  credits: box SDF after I. Quilez, ACES fit by K. Narkowicz,
  hashes by D. Hoskins and M. O'Neill (PCG), FDN reverb after
  Jot & Chaigne, phasing after S. Reich, growing dominoes
  after L. Whitehead. Loader from Latent's Turbo Boost.

